{"base_rate":0.5443234836702955,"brier":0.2554088646967341,"bss":-0.029727349585568108,"bss_hi":0.06028578858049228,"bss_lo":-0.15662666043724666,"chart":{"base":[767.8,80.0],"fp":[376.1,257.6],"lead":"62,262.4 272,259.3 482,253.7 692,227.1","note":{"base":"skill -0.03 — higher than 11% of cities","fp":"low end +17pp, high end +25pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.0 °C — better than 67% of cities","rel":"promised 22% → rained 28%; promised 98% → rained 78%"},"rel":"200.5,343.5 456.6,318.7 600.8,240.9 680.2,130.7"},"country":"TT","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.22104199066874036,"ess":368.55409149682976,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Port of Spain</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Port of Spain rain forecast is cannot beat its own climatology, though 7 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>82%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(11%), there is still roughly a <b>26%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 643 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-25. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 20.7 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score -0.03, ranked 189 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(179&ndash;199) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>11%</td><td class='num'><b>26%</b></td><td class='num'>61</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'><b>30%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>53%</td><td class='num'><b>26%</b></td><td class='num'>65</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>72%</td><td class='num'><b>42%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>82%</td><td class='num'><b>45%</b></td><td class='num'>53</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>88%</td><td class='num'><b>58%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>94%</td><td class='num'><b>62%</b></td><td class='num'>63</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>82%</b></td><td class='num'>205</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">7 of 8 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Port of Spain</b> <span class=\"muted\">Trinidad and Tobago</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Cannot beat climatology</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">7 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>-0.03</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>179&ndash;199\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>643 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Port of Spain &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Port of Spain\"><rect cla