\" cy=\"228.4375\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 82%&amp;#10;It rained 45% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 53 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"349.2150943396227\" cy=\"217.16981132075472\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 88%&amp;#10;It rained 58% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 66 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"370.05636363636364\" cy=\"172.4242424242424\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 94%&amp;#10;It rained 62% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 63 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"390.9847619047619\" cy=\"156.66666666666666\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 82% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 205 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"409.7723902439025\" cy=\"81.92195121951221\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(54%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Port of Spain the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.01) and least in\n<b>autumn</b> (-0.14).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>163</td><td class='num'>55%</td><td class='num'>-0.137</td><td class='num'>26.6%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>145</td><td class='num'>43%</td><td class='num'>-0.096</td><td class='num'>21.0%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>174</td><td class='num'>68%</td><td class='num'>-0.019</td><td class='num'>15.7%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>161</td><td class='num'>50%</td><td class='num'>-0.014</td><td class='num'>21.0%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":10.66668,"lon":-61.51889,"n":643,"n_cities":213,"name":"Port of Spain","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.24,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.10918032786885244,"n":61,"obs":0.26229508196721313,"sig":true},{"hi":0.43,"lo":0.24,"mean":0.321969696969697,"n":66,"obs":0.30303030303030304,"sig":false},{"hi":0.65,"lo":0.43,"mean":0.5323076923076924,"n":65,"obs":0.26153846153846155,"sig":true},{"hi":0.79,"lo":0.65,"mean":0.72171875,"n":64,"obs":0.421875,"sig":true},{"hi":0.86,"lo":0.79,"mean":0.8226415094339623,"n":53,"obs":0.4528301886792453,"sig":true},{"hi":0.92,"lo":0.86,"mean":0.8815151515151516,"n":66,"obs":0.5757575757575758,"sig":true},{"hi":0.97,"lo":0.92,"mean":0.9406349206349206,"n":63,"obs":0.6190476190476191,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.97,"mean":0.993707317073171,"n":205,"obs":0.824390243902439,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":20.7,"provisional":false,"rank":189,"rank_hi":199.0,"rank_lo":179.0,"reliability":0.058762286431161076,"resolution":0.049443868900608076,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"port-of-spain","station":"","timezone":"America/Port_of_Spain"}